<title>USA: U.S. House bids farewell to TV-bound Molinari.</title>
<headline>U.S. House bids farewell to TV-bound Molinari.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The House of Representatives bid farewell on Thursday to Susan Molinari, half of its only husband-wife legislative team, who is heading for a job in television.</p>
<p>Molinari, a moderate New York Republican, announced in May she was quitting politics to become a co-anchor of a new CBS Saturday morning news show.</p>
<p>Moments after an historic tax cut vote, the House began paying tribute to Molinari, who cried and hugged colleagues.</p>
<p>&quot;I never thought I'd come to the day when I'd say I love a member of the press -- but I love you, Susan,&quot; said her husband and self-described &quot;legislative pal,&quot; New York Republican Representative Bill Paxon.</p>
</text>
